[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-e84f2a94-ca2f-4ef0-97ce-1d1168909e0c\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research papers</p><strong>Fri 9 Oct 2026 13:48 - 14:06 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/issta-2026/splash-issta-2026-venue-east-hall-1\" class=\"room-link navigate\">East Hall 1</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Mobile and Software Security</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/jordansamhi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Jordan Samhi</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"e84f2a94-ca2f-4ef0-97ce-1d1168909e0c\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Ghosts in the Memory: Detecting Unintended Sensitive Data in Android Apps</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Android apps often retain sensitive information such as co-users\u2019 data, authentication tokens, and encryption keys in memory, leaving them vulnerable to unauthorized access. Existing dynamic analysis tools struggle to detect such memory-resident leaks because of three fundamental challenges: \\textit{(i)} runtime application self-protection (RASP) and other anti-analysis mechanisms actively detect and block conventional instrumentation; \\textit{(ii)} the semantic gap between high-level data types and their raw memory representations obscures sensitive content; and \\textit{(iii)} the transient nature of memory-resident data causes snapshot-based methods to miss critical exposures. We present ANDROID-MRI, an OS-level analysis tool that embeds tracing directly into the Android kernel to detect unintended sensitive data leakage through memory while remaining invisible to application-layer defenses. ANDROID-MRI provides instruction-granular monitoring to track the propagation of sensitive data in memory, surfacing the full context of unintended persistence. In an evaluation of 50 popular apps (\u22651M installs), ANDROID-MRI bypassed 97.6% of RASP protections (vs. 52.4% for Frida) and revealed 17 previously unknown memory disclosures. These included leaks of profile PINs, subscription-only content, and cryptographic keys. 12 vendors confirmed the issues; 4 have patched them, and 3 (Netflix, Smule, and Delivery Express) acknowledged them via bug bounty programs.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/seonghyeonsong\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Seonghyeon Song<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sungkyunkwan University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/kimtaeyoung1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Taeyoung Kim<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sungkyunkwan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>South Korea</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/woojookim\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Woojoo Kim<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sungkyunkwan University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/seojinpark\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Seojin Park<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sungkyunkwan University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/sungjaehwang1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Sungjae Hwang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/sungjaehwang1/d5f16778-76ad-43fa-9a70-e6496c63e6b0/micro-avatar?1792875589000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Sungjae Hwang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sungkyunkwan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Republic of Korea</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/hyoungshickkim\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Hyoungshick Kim\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/hyoungshickkim/3fc68534-1eb9-479e-ab07-3c1c7a23e972/micro-avatar?1792875581000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Hyoungshick Kim<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sungkyunkwan University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Republic of Korea</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/107/Ghosts-in-the-Memory-Detecting-Unintended-Sensitive-Data-in-Android-Apps\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-e84f2a94-ca2f-4ef0-97ce-1d1168909e0c').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
